WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:16.187
<v Host>Welcome to Japanese Daily News. I'm Maya. Today is June seventeenth. The price of chicken in Japan has climbed to its highest level on record — and a weaker yen is a big part of the reason. Let's listen.

00:00:16.788 --> 00:00:19.547
<v News>今日のニュースです。

00:00:20.248 --> 00:00:26.032
<v News>鶏肉の値段が、今までで一番高くなりました。

00:00:26.731 --> 00:00:35.707
<v News>国の調査によると、鶏肉100グラムの平均の値段は、157円でした。

00:00:36.408 --> 00:00:44.231
<v News>これは、2015年に記録をとり始めてから、一番高い値段です。

00:00:44.932 --> 00:00:50.164
<v News>値段が上がった理由の一つは、円安です。

00:00:50.863 --> 00:00:57.631
<v News>円が安いと、外国から買うニワトリのエサが高くなります。

00:00:58.332 --> 00:01:05.676
<v News>エサが高くなると、鶏肉を作るお金も増えて、値段が上がります。

00:01:06.376 --> 00:01:13.647
<v News>牛肉や、外国から運ばれる肉の値段も、高くなっています。

00:01:14.347 --> 00:01:21.715
<v News>毎日の食事を作る家庭にとって、厳しい状況が続いています。

00:01:22.415 --> 00:01:29.760
<v News>お店では、少しでも安い肉を選ぶお客さんが増えているそうです。

00:01:30.459 --> 00:01:32.091
<v Host>Let's break it down.

00:01:32.691 --> 00:01:39.292
<v Slow>鶏肉の値段が、今までで一番高くなりました。

00:01:40.091 --> 00:01:43.739
<v Host>The price of chicken has become the highest it has ever been.

00:01:44.340 --> 00:01:46.427
<v Vocab>値段

00:01:46.828 --> 00:01:54.507
<v Host>It means price — how much something costs. A very everyday word; you'll see it on every shelf and menu.

00:01:55.108 --> 00:02:05.379
<v Slow>国の調査によると、鶏肉100グラムの平均の値段は、157円でした。

00:02:06.180 --> 00:02:13.907
<v Host>According to a national survey, the average price of one hundred grams of chicken was one hundred fifty-seven yen.

00:02:14.508 --> 00:02:16.692
<v Vocab>調査

00:02:17.092 --> 00:02:25.348
<v Host>It means a survey or investigation — looking into something carefully. The government does one to track prices across the whole country.

00:02:25.948 --> 00:02:34.900
<v Slow>これは、2015年に記録をとり始めてから、一番高い値段です。

00:02:35.699 --> 00:02:40.644
<v Host>This is the highest price since they began keeping records in twenty fifteen.

00:02:41.243 --> 00:02:43.475
<v Vocab>記録

00:02:43.876 --> 00:02:51.580
<v Host>It means a record — written-down data, or a best-ever mark in sports. Here it's the kept data on prices over the years.

00:02:52.180 --> 00:02:58.156
<v Slow>値段が上がった理由の一つは、円安です。

00:02:58.955 --> 00:03:01.764
<v Host>One reason the price went up is the weak yen.

00:03:02.364 --> 00:03:04.812
<v Vocab>円安

00:03:05.211 --> 00:03:16.324
<v Host>It means a weak yen — when the yen is worth less against other money. The first character is yen, the second means cheap. A cheap yen makes imports expensive.

00:03:16.924 --> 00:03:24.651
<v Slow>円が安いと、外国から買うニワトリのエサが高くなります。

00:03:25.451 --> 00:03:30.611
<v Host>When the yen is cheap, the chicken feed bought from abroad becomes more expensive.

00:03:31.211 --> 00:03:33.228
<v Vocab>エサ

00:03:33.627 --> 00:03:41.764
<v Host>It means feed or food for animals. Much of Japan's chicken feed is imported, so its cost rides on the exchange rate.

00:03:42.364 --> 00:03:50.668
<v Slow>牛肉や、外国から運ばれる肉の値段も、高くなっています。

00:03:51.467 --> 00:03:56.484
<v Host>Beef, and meat brought in from abroad, are also getting more expensive.

00:03:57.084 --> 00:03:59.508
<v Vocab>牛肉

00:03:59.907 --> 00:04:08.163
<v Host>It means beef. The first character is cow, the second is meat. The same pattern gives you chicken meat and pork.

00:04:08.764 --> 00:04:17.187
<v Slow>毎日の食事を作る家庭にとって、厳しい状況が続いています。

00:04:17.987 --> 00:04:23.052
<v Host>For households that cook every day, a tough situation continues.

00:04:23.651 --> 00:04:26.052
<v Vocab>厳しい

00:04:26.451 --> 00:04:35.211
<v Host>It means strict, harsh, or tough. Here it describes a hard, demanding situation — a hard time for the family budget.

00:04:35.812 --> 00:04:44.211
<v Slow>お店では、少しでも安い肉を選ぶお客さんが増えているそうです。

00:04:45.012 --> 00:04:50.052
<v Host>At the shops, it's said more customers are choosing even slightly cheaper meat.

00:04:50.651 --> 00:04:52.788
<v Vocab>選ぶ

00:04:53.187 --> 00:04:59.740
<v Host>It means to choose, to pick. When prices rise, shoppers carefully choose the cheaper option.

00:05:00.339 --> 00:05:03.339
<v Host>Let's listen to the full story one more time.

00:05:03.939 --> 00:05:06.699
<v News>今日のニュースです。

00:05:07.399 --> 00:05:13.184
<v News>鶏肉の値段が、今までで一番高くなりました。

00:05:13.884 --> 00:05:22.860
<v News>国の調査によると、鶏肉100グラムの平均の値段は、157円でした。

00:05:23.560 --> 00:05:31.384
<v News>これは、2015年に記録をとり始めてから、一番高い値段です。

00:05:32.084 --> 00:05:37.315
<v News>値段が上がった理由の一つは、円安です。

00:05:38.016 --> 00:05:44.783
<v News>円が安いと、外国から買うニワトリのエサが高くなります。

00:05:45.483 --> 00:05:52.827
<v News>エサが高くなると、鶏肉を作るお金も増えて、値段が上がります。

00:05:53.528 --> 00:06:00.800
<v News>牛肉や、外国から運ばれる肉の値段も、高くなっています。

00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:08.867
<v News>毎日の食事を作る家庭にとって、厳しい状況が続いています。

00:06:09.567 --> 00:06:16.911
<v News>お店では、少しでも安い肉を選ぶお客さんが増えているそうです。

00:06:17.612 --> 00:06:20.348
<v Host>Quiz time. Three questions.

00:06:20.947 --> 00:06:27.860
<v Slow>鶏肉の値段は、今までと比べてどうなりましたか。

00:06:28.660 --> 00:06:33.411
<v Host>How does the price of chicken compare to before? It became the highest ever.

00:06:34.012 --> 00:06:40.875
<v Slow>鶏肉100グラムの平均の値段は、いくらでしたか。

00:06:41.675 --> 00:06:47.531
<v Host>What was the average price of one hundred grams of chicken? One hundred fifty-seven yen.

00:06:48.132 --> 00:06:53.795
<v Slow>値段が上がった理由の一つは、何ですか。

00:06:54.596 --> 00:06:58.076
<v Host>What is one reason the price went up? The weak yen.

00:06:58.675 --> 00:07:11.060
<v Host>That's today's Japanese Daily News. Full transcript with furigana at podcast.jpnotes.dev. Subscribe on Apple Podcasts or Spotify. See you tomorrow.

00:07:11.660 --> 00:07:13.915
<v News>また明日。
